{
 "voice": "am_puck",
 "duration": 65.975,
 "lines": [
  {
   "line": 0,
   "text": "A London skyscraper melted a parked car without ever touching it.",
   "start": 0.25,
   "end": 4.155
  },
  {
   "line": 1,
   "text": "It's twenty thirteen, and the City's shiny new tower isn't even finished yet.",
   "start": 4.595,
   "end": 8.875
  },
  {
   "line": 2,
   "text": "Down below, a man parks his Jaguar on the street and pops out for an hour.",
   "start": 9.155,
   "end": 13.46
  },
  {
   "line": 3,
   "text": "When he comes back, the wing mirror and the badge have melted.",
   "start": 13.7,
   "end": 16.82
  },
  {
   "line": 4,
   "text": "The next day, a reporter puts a frying pan on the pavement, cracks an egg into it, and it fries.",
   "start": 17.18,
   "end": 22.66
  },
  {
   "line": 5,
   "text": "Across the road, a barber's doormat starts to smoke.",
   "start": 22.94,
   "end": 25.795
  },
  {
   "line": 6,
   "text": "Then somebody finally looks up.",
   "start": 26.155,
   "end": 27.985
  },
  {
   "line": 7,
   "text": "The whole glass front of the tower is pointing one blazing spot of sunlight straight at the street.",
   "start": 28.225,
   "end": 33.48
  },
  {
   "line": 8,
   "text": "Luckily, nobody got hurt.",
   "start": 33.92,
   "end": 35.5
  },
  {
   "line": 9,
   "text": "Unluckily, the egg did.",
   "start": 35.82,
   "end": 37.2
  },
  {
   "line": 10,
   "text": "Ever used a magnifying glass to focus the sun into one tiny burning dot?",
   "start": 37.68,
   "end": 42.385
  },
  {
   "line": 11,
   "text": "This tower's face curves inwards like a giant mirror, so every window bounces its sunlight to the same patch of road.",
   "start": 42.625,
   "end": 49.455
  },
  {
   "line": 12,
   "text": "So the owners bolted a huge sunshade of metal fins across the front, and London's newest landmark had to wear sunglasses.",
   "start": 49.815,
   "end": 57.235
  },
  {
   "line": 13,
   "text": "And the architect? He'd seen this before.",
   "start": 57.675,
   "end": 60.245
  },
  {
   "line": 14,
   "text": "His hotel in Las Vegas had already been melting tourists' shopping bags by the pool.",
   "start": 60.485,
   "end": 65.415
  }
 ],
